# Skill execution (installed skills)

Task is **not** complete until:

| Skill | Done when |
|-------|-----------|
| **excalidraw-diagram** | Node-to-node arrows have both bindings and reciprocal endpoint references; architecture routing uses clear horizontal/vertical lanes, with no preventable crossings; icon captions leave connection points clear. Every Azure service node uses its official icon from the bundled SVG cache, or a labeled box reported in the reply when the cache has none. F5, Palo Alto Networks, NGINX, and Datadog nodes use the cached Simple Icons SVGs from `vendor-icons.md`. `.excalidraw` → PNG under the 30,000-patch vision cap, images **viewed** (crop grown regions when editing), layout fixed; existing files: collision pass before first PNG |
| **word-document** | DOCX validates; explicit table styling (docx-js) or one python-docx path; deliver **`.docx` only** (no generator beside deliverable unless user asks) |
| **word-document (no npm)** | python-docx + `validate`; note fallback in reply; `bash scripts/install_deps.sh office` |
| **powerpoint-presentation** | PPTX validates; **`thumbnail` every deck** (grid + `--per-slide` 150 DPI), images **viewed**, overflow fixed; `office-system` installed if missing; test native PowerPoint opening when available, otherwise report it unverified; follow repair-prompt recovery in the skill |
| **powerpoint-presentation (no npm)** | Template/XML path only — **no** greenfield deck; do not claim new-deck delivery without pptxgenjs or user template; preview still mandatory if `.pptx` delivered |
| **spreadsheet-document** | `.xlsx` delivered; formulas LibreOffice can evaluate (no `XLOOKUP`/`XMATCH`/`SORT`/`FILTER`/`UNIQUE`/`SEQUENCE`; `_xlfn.` prefix where required); if formulas used: `office_tools.py recalc` → JSON `status: success` (zero formula errors; `status: success` is not proof the numbers are right); external-link refusal is a failed recalc until cached values are preserved or `--force`; `office-system` for recalc |
| **pdf-document** | Deliver requested `.pdf`; form fills: run validation scripts per `references/forms.md` |
| **verification-before-completion** | No completion/success claim without fresh verification command output in the same message |
| **newagentlink** | `/tmp/<topic>-newagentlink.md` written once this turn; one-shot banner present; live git gathered; chat returns path + starter prompt only; never writes `/tmp/<topic>-handoff.md` |
| **api-and-interface-design** | Contract defined before implementation; consistent errors; validation at boundaries; pagination on lists; cross-check against `deprecation-and-migration` when changing public interfaces |
| **github-markdown** | Render context identified; valid GFM syntax; context-limited features avoided (e.g. no footnotes in wikis); relative in-repo links where applicable; delivery checklist in `SKILL.md` satisfied |
| **deprecation-and-migration** | Replacement exists before deprecation; migration guide with concrete steps; usage verified at zero before removal; formal deliverables use `word-document` when requested |
| **terraform-commit-review** | Commit range established; every changed file read; provider docs verified via MCP (Context7 + Microsoft Learn); all 7 checklist sections applied (correctness, security/RBAC, destructive changes, naming, cross-phase, code quality, documentation/runbook); structured report with intent summary, per-phase table, issues by severity, vendor-ready comments, source URLs, and execution summary when no apply blockers |
| **terraform-apply-assistance** | Apply scope established (commit hash through HEAD or inferred); error/plan triaged; stayed on the current working branch (new branch only when the current branch is `main`, or the user asks); diagnosis backed by Context7 + Microsoft Learn MCP; smallest correct edit applied; local validation run (fmt, validate, diff --check); **paused for user review** — no commit/push unless user explicitly instructs; plan evaluated with rubric (OK / conditionally OK / not OK); recap/runbook requests honor phase scope exclusions; unresolved risks re-raised every iteration; execution summary with apply decision, global/common/phase-specific env prerequisites, per-phase `## Phase N` command blocks, and post-apply checks |
| **mcp-tool-rules** | MCP config read; servers presented to user and confirmed; tools discovered per server; editor-appropriate files generated (Cursor: `.mdc` rules, Copilot: `.instructions.md`) with parameter tables and example calls; all files validated (server names match config case-sensitive, every tool has table + example, frontmatter valid); report delivered listing files generated, servers/tools documented, and any skipped tools or failed servers |
| **security-audit** | All 6 phases completed (Recon → Hunt → Validate → Report → Structured output → Independent verification); `findings.json` validates against schema (`validate-findings.cjs`); `REPORT.md` and `FINDINGS-DETAIL.md` reconciled with `findings.json`; output directory contains all artifacts (`architecture.md`, `REPORT.md`, `FINDINGS-DETAIL.md`, `findings.json`) |
| **context7-docs** | Library/framework docs fetched via Context7 MCP (`user-context7` in Cursor, `context7` in Copilot); version-specific library ID selected when applicable; query decomposed to one topic per call; source cited in response; fallback to web search or Microsoft Learn when Context7 lacks the library |
| **notion-mcp-ops** | Notion MCP server discovered with correct editor server name; fetch before write on updates; anchors from fetched content; formatting rules applied (`<callout>`, HTML tables); post-update verify fetch for structural edits; property names from fetched schema |

**PowerPoint is not done** when the `.pptx` exists—only after layout preview (or user waives visual QA).

Structural validation, rendered layout, and native PowerPoint opening are separate checks. LibreOffice rendering does not prove Microsoft PowerPoint compatibility. After a repair prompt, preserve the original and verify content, presenter notes and layout before replacing it; claim native opening only after a client test or user confirmation. See [the recovery workflow](../../skills/powerpoint-presentation/references/layout-preview.md#microsoft-powerpoint-compatibility).

Artifact skills (Word, PPT, XLSX, PDF) require **verification-before-completion** before delivery claims.

- **PPT:** LibreOffice Impress + Poppler every delivery → `bash scripts/install_deps.sh office-system`
- **DOCX preview:** LibreOffice Writer + Poppler. `bash scripts/runtime_readiness.sh --require-office` must pass for DOCX/PPTX readiness; it checks offline schemas, validation, and actual conversion outputs. Calc and spreadsheet recalculation are not checked.
- **Word (new):** `bash scripts/install_deps.sh node` for docx-js; without npm → python-docx via `bash scripts/install_deps.sh office`
- **PPT (new):** `bash scripts/install_deps.sh node` for pptxgenjs only — no python greenfield fallback
- **Excalidraw:** Playwright via `bash scripts/install_deps.sh excalidraw`

## Custom agents (installed library)

Applies when the user invokes a custom agent or you test agent behavior in this repo:

| Agent | Done when |
|-------|-----------|
| **code-review** | Scope established (SHA range when provided); tests reviewed first; five-axis review; requirements alignment when plan supplied; logic traced; Strengths + findings with file:line evidence; verification story; MCP/web verification table; merge verdict (Yes/No/With fixes); **no source files edited** |
| **security-auditor** | Scope established; trust boundaries + STRIDE; findings by severity with file:line evidence; PoC for Critical/High; MCP/web verification when applicable; release verdict (Yes/No/With fixes); **no source files edited** |

After editing `agents/`, run `bash scripts/install_library.sh agents cursor` so global `~/.cursor/agents/` matches repo source.
After editing `user-rules/cursor/`, run `bash scripts/install_library.sh rules cursor` so `~/.cursor/rules/` matches repo source.
Do not hand-edit `user-rules/copilot/`. After editing `user-rules/cursor/`, run `bash scripts/sync_copilot_rules.sh` to regenerate the Copilot fragments, then `bash scripts/install_library.sh rules copilot` so `~/.copilot/copilot-instructions.md` is rebuilt.

## Review handoff (skill + always-on trigger)

Canonical protocol: `skills/review-handoff/SKILL.md` (Cursor and Copilot only, via `EDITOR_VARIANT_SKILLS`; loaded on demand). Always-on trigger: `user-rules/cursor/review-handoff-reconciliation.mdc` (installs to `~/.cursor/rules/`) and the generated `user-rules/copilot/review-handoff.md` (concatenated into `~/.copilot/copilot-instructions.md`). The trigger only tells the agent to read the skill. Do not duplicate the body here or in the trigger.

| Work | Done when |
|------|-----------|
| **review-handoff** | `/tmp/<topic>-handoff.md` **appended** this turn (no full-file overwrite, truncate, or delete of prior rounds; surgical header Status/Must fix only); dispositions used (FIX / DEFER / KEEP / DO NOT APPLY / FIXED / RECONCILED); chat points at the path; reviewer does not mutate the review repo (only the `/tmp` handoff). Distinct from `newagentlink` (`/tmp/<topic>-newagentlink.md`). |

