Canonical sources: `user-rules/cursor/branch-strategy.mdc` (installs to `~/.cursor/rules/`) and `user-rules/copilot/branch-strategy.md` (concatenated into `~/.copilot/copilot-instructions.md`). Do not duplicate the body here.

| Work | Done when |
|------|-----------|
| **branch-strategy** | One working branch at a time (the branch already checked out). No edit, commit, or push on `main`. No switch off a branch that still has unmerged commits or uncommitted files. A new branch only when the current branch is `main`, or the user asks, and it is created from `main`. Mixed topics on one branch are expected. Pause before `git commit` or `git push`. |

